 to do is  limit that in order to reduce cost the  other reason I wouldn't  start doing means-testing for these  programs is that you create stigma  around claiming of the benefits okay if  you have too much money and you don't  qualify it starts to imply that by  receiving a social benefit you're sort  of branding yourself in a particular way  which people may not really want to do  for better or worse that could be  something we say it shouldn't be that  way but it is there is stigma around  some of these programs so what you end  up doing really is increasing the cost  of the programs and diverting money away  from the money that could actually go to  people by having these means testing  apparatus and when you means test it's  known to hurt those in the middle  because when there's a cut-off point  people on the sort of borderline will  start to make financial decisions in  order not to start losing benefits by  going above what those limits are it  creates this gaming mentality the stigma  component so I'm against it I understand  morally the reason why many people would  look at that I don't think it's a good  idea I don't think it's something that  the left should run on if you disagree  let me know we've got a great bonus show  for you today three great stories and  more david pakman.com slash membership  patreon.com slash david pakman show to  get instant access to the bonus show
 

